From 51af10381a185d6138f84ed2caf7076d381ec1d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:56:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/40] drm/gma500: add the sgxfive render node with queries
 and buffers

Expose the SGX545 to unprivileged userspace through a render node with the
sgxfive interface (include/uapi/drm/sgxfive_drm.h): DEV_QUERY for the core
identity and quirks, the loaded firmware, the client heap layout (the DDK's
REV1 table, with the shader heaps limited to the windows code can reach and
the firmware heaps reserved), job limits and tiling; CREATE_BO for shmem
buffers mapped write-combined; GET_BO_MMAP_OFFSET for buffers created with CPU
access. VM, context and job ioctls answer -EOPNOTSUPP until they exist.

gma500 has no ioctls of its own, so the sgxfive ones become the driver's,
routed through gma_sgx.c; the SGX device is now created at probe. Buffer
pages come from lowmem: the shmem helper sets a write-combined BO's kernel
mapping WC on first use, and set_pages_array_wc() oopses on HIGHMEM pages,
which a 32-bit kernel with 2 GiB hands out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
